    <item>
      <pubDate>Fri, 28 Nov 2025 10:08:08 -0600</pubDate>
      <title>You're invited!</title>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">66940469</guid>
      <link>https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/OHCCC/bulletins/3fd6e35</link>
      <description>
        <![CDATA[<p><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"><img src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/OHCCC/2017/11/2390784/govdelivery-neighborhoods-original-original-origina_original.png" alt="Department of Neighborhoods" title="null" width="600" height="225" /></span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"><img src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/OHCCC/2025/11/12758520/don-ubuntu-emailgraphic-december-2025_original.jpg" alt="Ubuntu session Dec. 4, 2025" title="Ubuntu session Dec. 4, 2025" width="600" height="600" style="float: left;" /></span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"><br />Dear Community Leaders, Partners and Friends,<br /><br /></span><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">The Department of Neighborhoods will host its fourth 2025 session of the Ubuntu Series: Unity Conversations Across Cultures. The theme is <strong>&ldquo;Building Bridges: Celebrating New Americans in Columbus</strong>&rdquo;.&nbsp; This session is designed to foster collaboration and promote inclusion, belonging and access to opportunities through civic engagement and shared storytelling. <br /><br /></span><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">We are pleased to announce that we will have leaders from the following organizations leading discussions:<br /><br /></span><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">Community Refugee and Immigration Services (CRIS), Ethiopian Tewahedo Social Services (ETSS), and Jewish and Family Services (JFS) to share valuable expertise, lived experience that will help anchor our dialogue and inspire meaning action. <br /><br /></span><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">To contribute or learn from this last 2025 session of our Unity Conversations series, please register to secure your seat by&nbsp; clicking </span><a href="https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/51a4315affc74bbd8ad96e8656a11345?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery"><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">here</span></a><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"> or scanning the QR code on the flyer. The earlier you complete your registration, the better, as we anticipate having more participants. <br /><br /></span><strong><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">When</span></strong><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">: Thursday, Dec. 4, 2025</span></p>
<p><strong><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">Where</span></strong><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">: Glenwood Community Center at 1888 Fairmount Ave., Columbus, OH 43223</span></p>
<p><strong><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">Time:</span></strong><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"> 5:00 pm to 7:30 pm<br /><br /></span><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">Please share with your networks. This event is free and open to the public. See attached flyer for additional details. If you have any questions, <strong><u>contact Lindora Howard-Diawara at </u></strong></span><a href="mailto:LKDiawara@columbus.gov"><strong><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">LKDiawara@columbus.gov</span></strong></a><strong><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"> or 614-645-3284</span></strong><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">.<br /><br /></span><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;">Thank you!</span></p>]]>
      </description>
    </item>
